BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260924T180623Z
DTSTART:20260912T190000Z
DTEND:20260913T190000Z
SUMMARY:San Francisco Moby-Dick Marathon 2026
DESCRIPTION:FREE\n\nCo-presented with the San Francisco Maritime National Park Association and the San Francisco Maritime National Historical Park\n\nThis nonstop\, cover-to-cover reading transforms the San Francisco Maritime Museum into the setting for one of the city's most beloved literary traditions! Steeped in maritime history\, theatrical creativity\, and community participation\, the&nbsp\;Moby-Dick&nbsp\;Marathon brings Melville's monumental novel to life in a way that is lively\, accessible\, and\, dare we say\, fun. Literary thrill-seekers gather annually to celebrate this complicated\, provocative\, much-beloved-and-sometimes-dreaded epic of nautical life! Volunteer readers of all backgrounds\, from special guest performers to members of the public\, lend their voices to the story chapter by chapter. This year's MD24 blends San Francisco's creative spirit with live performance\, visual art\, spectacle\, and surprise\, creating an unforgettable celebration of one of America's greatest novels. Come for a chapter\, stay for the night\, or experience the full 24 hours inside the spectacularly restored Art Deco landmark that is the Maritime Museum!
CATEGORIES:FICTION
LOCATION:San Francisco Maritime Museum\, 900 Beach St\, San Francisco
SEQUENCE:0
UID:907802ac8b1aec81472057368444931c
